<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaolack</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaolack is a city in west-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> on the Saloum river, capital of Kaolack Region. Founded near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahone">Kahone</a>, the old capital of the kingdom of Saloum, it grew under French rule from the late 19th century into the country's main centre of the groundnut trade, served by rail and a river port. It is also an important religious centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tijaniyya">Tijaniyya</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> order.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kaolack.jpg" alt="Kaolack" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photograph by Joseph Hill, 2001, who contributed the photo with the condition that it be attributed. · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MedinaBaayMosque.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
